[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m Given the polynomial \(x^2 + rx + s\) with roots \(s\) and \(t\), we use Vieta's formulas:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m - The sum of the roots: \(s + t = -r\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m - The product of the roots: \(s \cdot t = s\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m From the product of the roots, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m \[ s \cdot t = s \implies s(t - 1) = 0 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m Since \(s \neq 0\), we have \(t = 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m For the polynomial \(x^2 + tx + r\) with root 5, we use Vieta's formulas:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m - The sum of the roots: \(5 + u = -t\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m - The product of the roots: \(5 \cdot u = r\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m Substituting \(t = 1\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m \[ 5 + u = -1 \implies u = -6 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m Thus, \(r = 5u = 5(-6) = -30\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m Using the sum of the roots for the first polynomial:
