[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m We need to find the sum of the positive divisors of \(362880\) that have units digit 1. A number ending in 1 must be congruent to 1 modulo 10. 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m The divisors of \(362880\) that are congruent to 1 modulo 10 must satisfy the conditions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 1. They must be odd (so no factor of 2).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 2. They must be congruent to 1 modulo 5.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m We consider the form of the divisors as \(3^b \times 5^c \times 7^d\) where \(0 \leq b \leq 4\), \(0 \leq c \leq 1\), and \(0 \leq d \leq 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m We check the conditions for each case:
