[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m To solve the problem of finding the sum of the positive divisors of \(9!\) that have units digit 1, we start by noting that \(9! = 362880\). We need to consider the prime factorization of \(9!\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m \[ 9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5 \times 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m We are looking for the sum of the divisors of \(9!\) that have a units digit of 1. These divisors must satisfy the condition \(d \equiv 1 \pmod{10}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m The divisors of \(9!\) can be written as \(2^a \times 3^b \times 5^c \times 7^d\) where \(0 \leq a \leq 7\), \(0 \leq b \leq 4\), \(c \in \{0, 1\}\), and \(0 \leq d \leq 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m We need to check the conditions modulo 10:
