[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m Aya walks 9 kilometers every morning and stops at a coffee shop. When she walks at a constant speed of \( s \) kilometers per hour, the total time including \( t \) minutes spent in the coffee shop is 4 hours. When she increases her speed to \( s + 2 \) kilometers per hour, the total time including \( t \) minutes is 2 hours and 24 minutes (which is 2.4 hours). We need to find the time it takes her to walk if she walks at \( s + \frac{1}{2} \) kilometers per hour.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=191960)[0m 
